    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters August 17 with a high-upside offensive slate, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (69.89) and **Austin Riley** (66.15). **Corbin Carroll** remains our premier start; despite a negative platoon shift against Alec Gamboa, his elite sprint speed and elevated park factor in this matchup provide the highest ceiling on the roster. **Austin Riley** earns a massive +19% boost from the matchup against Bailey Ober, whose high xERA suggests a prime opportunity for power production. While **Austin Riley** is hitting 8th, the favorable park environment and a 92% SB opportunity rate against Ober\u2019s delivery move him into must-start territory despite the lower order placement. **Seiya Suzuki** (61.27) is also a strong play, as the favorable park and batting order placement mitigate the danger posed by Luis Castillo.\n\nThe most difficult lineup decision involves **Mickey Moniak**, whose score of 45.58 barely keeps him in the UTIL slot. He faces a formidable hurdle in Blake Snell (2.39 xERA), and the -15% dynamic platoon hit is significant. However, the 14% park boost keeps him just above our \"below floor\" threshold, making him a marginal play. We are monitoring **Gabriel Moreno** (57.78) and **Henry Bolte** (57.18) closely; **Henry Bolte** is particularly intriguing given the 10% boost from the leadoff spot against Michael Wacha, providing necessary volume for our stolen base pursuit. We remain thin due to the absence of **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** on the IL, while **Josh Naylor** is unavailable today due to a team off-day. \n\nWe are keeping a close eye on the official lineups, as our current projections for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Mickey Moniak** are based on assumed batting orders. Should **Max Muncy** be pushed down the order further than his projected 7th spot, his already marginal 53.17 score could slip, potentially forcing a shuffle involving our deeper bench options like **Jose Caballero**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, or **Travis Bazzana**. With SB scarcity driving our strategy, any late-breaking news regarding weather or lineup changes will necessitate an immediate reassessment to protect our efficiency ratings.",
